1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,630
950 AIs searched for 21 hours… and
found a machine nobody had noticed.

2
00:00:07,800 --> 00:00:10,380
Picture the biggest library on Earth.

3
00:00:10,380 --> 00:00:12,780
Every book is written in DNA.

4
00:00:12,780 --> 00:00:16,820
And somewhere in there… is a
book nobody has ever read.

5
00:00:16,820 --> 00:00:19,200
So Anthropic sent in a search party:

6
00:00:19,200 --> 00:00:22,420
950 copies of its AI, Claude.

7
00:00:22,420 --> 00:00:26,300
They pulled more than 200,000
enzymes off the shelves.

8
00:00:26,300 --> 00:00:28,210
Kept 3,500.

9
00:00:28,210 --> 00:00:29,840
Then just 20.

10
00:00:29,840 --> 00:00:32,350
And one agent noticed something odd.

11
00:00:32,350 --> 00:00:36,950
Right next to an unusual enzyme…
a long row of repeating DNA,

12
00:00:36,950 --> 00:00:39,580
evenly spaced, like lines on a page.

13
00:00:39,580 --> 00:00:41,450
Here's why that's huge.

14
00:00:41,450 --> 00:00:44,530
That layout looks like CRISPR,
the gene-editing tool that won

15
00:00:44,530 --> 00:00:45,700
a Nobel Prize.

16
00:00:45,700 --> 00:00:48,250
So real scientists took it into the lab.

17
00:00:48,250 --> 00:00:52,300
And the repeats are copied into a
set of short RNA messages… just

18
00:00:52,300 --> 00:00:53,480
like CRISPR's.

19
00:00:53,480 --> 00:00:55,250
So what does it do?

20
00:00:55,550 --> 00:00:57,730
Nobody knows. Yet.

21
00:00:57,730 --> 00:01:00,850
It lives mainly in viruses
that infect bacteria.

22
00:01:00,850 --> 00:01:03,500
A CRISPR pioneer says
it's worth investigating.

23
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:07,190
Critics say a find with no known
job isn't a breakthrough yet.

24
00:01:07,190 --> 00:01:09,190
But here's the astonishing part.

25
00:01:09,190 --> 00:01:12,480
The humans wrote one prompt…
and did the lab work.

26
00:01:12,480 --> 00:01:13,470
The searching?

27
00:01:13,470 --> 00:01:14,740
That was the AI.

28
00:01:14,740 --> 00:01:18,240
So the next great discovery might
not start with "Eureka"… it

29
00:01:18,240 --> 00:01:21,020
might start with a search
party that never sleeps.

30
00:01:21,020 --> 00:01:23,850
Follow for more AI, explained like this.
